#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:1
msgid "Version 0.5.3 (2019-12-28)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:3
msgid ""
"Fixed: base64 encoded source maps now correctly decodes as utf-8. "
"Previously, non-ASCII characters could end up garbled. Thanks to ZHAO "
"Jinxiang (@xiaoxiangmoe)! (Note: This fix does not work in old "
"evironments not supporting both `TextDecoder` and `Uint8Array`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:7
msgid "Improved: Reduced size of the npm package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:9
msgid "Version 0.5.2 (2018-05-10)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:11
msgid ""
"Improved: Updated the version range of `atob` to disallow depending on "
"`2.0.3` which as a [security "
"vulnerability](https://snyk.io/test/npm/atob/2.0.3?severity=high&severity=medium&severity=low)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:15
msgid "Version 0.5.1 (2017-10-21)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:17
msgid ""
"Fixed: URLs are now decoded before being passed to `read` in Node.js. "
"This allows reading files with spaces, for example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:19
msgid ""
"Fixed: Missing or empty `sources` fields (such as `sources: []`) in "
"source maps are now handled. Previously, such source maps would cause "
"crashes or callbacks never bing called. Now, an empty result is produced:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:28
msgid "Version 0.5.0 (2016-02-28)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:30
msgid ""
"Improved: Errors now have a `sourceMapData` property that contain as much"
" as possible of the intended result of the function up until the error "
"occurred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:32
msgid ""
"Changed: `resolveSources` and `resolve`, as well as their `*Sync` "
"alternatives, no longer fail when one single source fails to be fetched. "
"Instead, the `sourcesContent` array in the result object will contain "
"error objects for all failed sources, and strings otherwise. (Backwards-"
"incompatible change.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:38
msgid "Version 0.4.0 (2015-08-29)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:40
msgid ""
"Removed: The `ignoreSourceRoot` option of `resolveSources`. It has been "
"replaced with `sourceRoot: false`. (Backwards-incompatible change.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:42
msgid ""
"Added: The `sourceRoot` option of `resolveSources`. It not only allows to"
" ignore the source root, it also lets you replace it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:44
msgid "Added: The `parseMapToJSON` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:45
msgid ""
"Added: The `resolve` method now accepts `null, mapUrl, ...` as arguments,"
" in addition to the existing signature, which will read `mapUrl` instead "
"of looking for a sourceMappingURL in the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:49
msgid "Version 0.3.1 (2014-08-16)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:51
msgid "Improved: Updated the source-map-url dependency to 0.3.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:54
msgid "Version 0.3.0 (2014-07-02)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:56
msgid ""
"Removed: Argument checking. It’s not worth it. (Possibly backwards-"
"incompatible change.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:58
msgid ""
"Added: The `sourceRoot` property of source maps may now be ignored, which"
" can be useful when resolving sources outside of the browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:60
msgid ""
"Added: It is now possible to resolve only the URLs of sources, without "
"reading them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:64
msgid "Version 0.2.0 (2014-06-22)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:66
msgid ""
"Changed: The result of `resolveSources` is now an object, not an array. "
"The old result array is available in the `sourcesContent` property. "
"(Backwards-incompatible change.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:69
msgid ""
"Changed: `sources` has been renamed to `sourcesContent` in the result "
"object of `resolve`. (Backwards-incompatible change.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:71
msgid ""
"Added: `resolveSources` now also returns all sources fully resolved, in "
"the `sourcesResolved` property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:73
msgid ""
"Added: The result object of `resolve` now contains the `sourcesResolved` "
"property from `resolveSources`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:77
msgid "Version 0.1.4 (2014-06-16)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:79
msgid ""
"Fixed: `sourcesContent` was mis-typed as `sourceContents`, which meant "
"that the `sourcesContent` property of source maps never was used when "
"resolving sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:84
msgid "Version 0.1.3 (2014-05-06)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:86
msgid "Only documentation and meta-data changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:89
msgid "Version 0.1.2 (2014-03-23)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:91
msgid ""
"Improved: Source maps starting with `)]}'` are now parsed correctly. The "
"spec allows source maps to start with that character sequence to prevent "
"XSSI attacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:96
msgid "Version 0.1.1 (2014-03-06)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:98
msgid "Improved: Make sourceRoot resolving more sensible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:100
msgid ""
"A source root such as `/scripts/subdir` is now treated as "
"`/scripts/subdir/` — that is, as a directory called “subdir”, not a file "
"called “subdir”. Pointing to a file as source root does not makes sense."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:106
msgid "Version 0.1.0 (2014-03-03)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_changelog.md:108
msgid "Initial release."
msgstr ""

